
#  rsyslog splitter ON DOCKER HOST 
Create /etc/rsyslog.d/30-modsec-split.conf on the host (use absolute paths):
Replace /ABS/PATH/TO with the real absolute path to your project (e.g., /srv/modsec-stack).


```ini
module(load="imfile")

# --- NGINX error.log → only hard blocks (“Access denied”) ---
input(type="imfile"
      File="/ABS/PATH/TO/logs/nginx/error.log"
      Tag="nginx-error:"
      addMetadata="on"
      ruleset="modsec_blocks")

ruleset(name="modsec_blocks") {
  if $msg contains "ModSecurity: Access denied" then {
    action(type="omfile" file="/ABS/PATH/TO/logs/modsec/blocked.log")
  }
  stop
}

# --- ModSecurity audit JSON → full detections stream ---
input(type="imfile"
      File="/ABS/PATH/TO/logs/modsec/audit.log"
      Tag="modsec-audit:"
      addMetadata="on"
      ruleset="modsec_detections")

ruleset(name="modsec_detections") {
  action(type="omfile" file="/ABS/PATH/TO/logs/modsec/detections.log")
}
```


Enable:
```bash
sudo systemctl restart rsyslog
```


## Logrotate (host)

/etc/logrotate.d/modsecurity:

```ini
/ABS/PATH/TO/logs/modsec/*.log {
  daily
  rotate 14
  missingok
  notifempty
  compress
  delaycompress
  create 0640 root root
  sharedscripts
  postrotate
    # poke nginx to reopen logs (safe even in container bind-mount case)
    /bin/kill -HUP $(pidof nginx) 2>/dev/null || true
  endscript
}



